---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="EV Trip Reports is a travel agent for EV road trips. Free corridor guides, custom plans a person reviews, and no payment from charging networks.">
  <section class="band band--tight">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1 class="h1">About</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:20px">EV Trip Reports is a travel agent for EVs. You tell us where you're going and what you drive. We plan the trip around charging.</p>
      <p>Free guides cover the corridors we publish. A paid plan is built for your car, adapter, memberships, and dates: charging options for that car, available backups, and any unverified gaps clearly marked. Detailed plans add estimated battery targets and sourced food, restroom, and lodging notes where available. A person reviews every plan before it reaches you. We don't book the hotel, the rental, or the ticket.</p>

      <h2>Who's behind it</h2>
      <p>I'm Zak Winnick. I work in EV charging infrastructure, and before that I spent 15 years in hospitality, mostly making sure guests didn't hit surprises. This site is the trip-planning version of that job.</p>
      <p>I started it because the charging details sit on a dozen network locators and forum threads. A guide puts the stall count, the kW, and who can use the site in one place, with a source and a check date on every fact.</p>

      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>No charging network pays for placement or coverage here, and none of them reviews a guide before it goes up. If a stop on a guide is a site I have a business connection to, that stop will say so.</p>
      <p>If we add affiliate links for hotels or gear, they will be marked where they appear. They will never decide which charger a guide recommends.</p>

      <h2>How the work gets done</h2>
      <p>AI tools do much of the research and upkeep: pulling station data, re-checking network locators, and collecting driver reports. The rules they follow are on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>. Facts get a source and a check date, or they get marked as not yet verified. A person reviews every custom plan before it is sent.</p>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <p>We don't book hotels, rental cars, or tickets. We don't label a charger fast or slow. The page gives kW and stall counts. PlugShare check-ins, X posts, and Reddit threads are driver reports. They are labeled as reports, and they are not treated as confirmed facts. Common questions are on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>.</p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>If you were at a stop recently and something doesn't match, we want to know. Use the correction link on the guide, or email <a href="mailto:admin@evtripreports.com">admin@evtripreports.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
